# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# coverage.py's data file: `just coverage` always leaves it (written by
# `coverage run`, read by `coverage report`).
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Virtual environments
.venv
.uv/

# Data warehouse & downloaded sources (regenerated by the pipeline)
data/*.duckdb
data/*.duckdb.wal
data/raw/
# Workbooks the seed scripts download (`scripts/build_*_seed*.py` without
# `--xlsx`). The seeds they produce are checked in; the sources are not.
data/*.xlsx
# Publishable artifact built by `just export-data`; it lives in GitHub releases
data/export/
# The retired hive Parquet archive. **Keep this entry**: older clones still have
# the directory on disk, and without it `git add -A` would stage it
# (`just clean` deletes it).
data/lake/
# Downloads kept between runs so a partitioned load does not re-fetch the retail
# zip per partition. Copies of what the URL serves — safe to delete.
data/cache/
# The course sandbox (`just course-sandbox`), a fixture warehouse the exercises
# break on purpose. Safe to delete.
data/course/
*.csv
!dbt/seeds/*.csv
# Unit-test fixtures are source, like the seeds. Without this line `dbt test`
# passes locally against files git never took, and CI fails.
!dbt/tests/fixtures/*.csv

# dbt
dbt/target/
dbt/dbt_packages/
dbt/logs/
dbt/.user.yml
# A lock dbt does not always remove after `dbt deps`.
dbt/package-lock.concurrent-update-lock

# dlt
.dlt/secrets.toml
**/.dlt/pipelines/

# Dagster instance: run/event storage, compute logs (DAGSTER_HOME).
# The checked-in dagster.yaml is config; everything beside it is state.
.dagster/*
!.dagster/dagster.yaml
.tmp_dagster_home_*/

# Evidence
reports/.evidence/
reports/build/
node_modules/

# Claude Code session transcripts and scratch notes: a local working record,
# never committed. What should outlive a session belongs in CLAUDE.md.
docs/sessions/

# The DuckLake landing zone, filled by `just ingest`. **Holds state no rebuild
# reproduces** — the snapshot lineage and the weather archive, which costs days
# of Open-Meteo's allowance to refetch — so `just clean` skips it.
data/lakehouse/
